++   `domain_verify`/`domain_connect` and FRONTEND-role behavior against
++   the prior pass's own claims.
++2. Found and fixed a real defect in
++   `app/deploy/adapters.py::VercelAdapter.get_domain_config()`:
++   `recommendedCNAME` target validation used a loose character class
++   (`[a-zA-Z0-9.-]{1,253}`) that accepted malformed hostnames (leading/
++   trailing hyphens, consecutive dots, bare hyphen labels) as a "valid"
++   DNS recommendation. Replaced with a strict per-label DNS-name regex
++   (`_valid_dns_target()`, same per-label discipline as
++   `valid_custom_hostname()` minus the reserved-TLD/vercel.app checks,
++   since this validates a Vercel-recommended CNAME target, not a
++   customer's own hostname claim). `recommendedCNAME`'s shape (a scalar
++   hostname string per entry) is unchanged and was already correctly
++   distinct from `recommendedIPv4`'s list-of-IPv4-strings shape — this
++   was a strictness fix, not a shape fix.
++3. Added `website-builder/tests/test_domain_prepare.py` (12 tests,
++   `pytest.mark.parametrize` combinations counted separately by the
++   runner as 23): drives `domain_prepare`/`domain_verify`/`domain_connect`
++   through the REAL `TelegramDispatcher` (not the orchestrator directly)
++   with a freshly-constructed `CustomDomainOrchestrator`/`ProjectStateStore`
