++   - `domain_prepare` never verifies/smokes/reaches `ATTACHED` even when
++     the remote DNS config is already fully ready and Vercel already
++     reports `verified=True` — proven across both `verified` boolean
++     values and both smoke-adapter-configured/unconfigured cases (4
++     parametrized combinations), asserting zero verify POSTs and no
++     smoke directory ever created.
++   - `domain_verify` on an unprepared project fails closed with
++     `DOMAIN_PREPARE_REQUIRED` even when the remote domain is already
++     bound and verified — verification is never a substitute for local
++     preparation history.
++   - A `domain_prepare` followed by a fresh-process `domain_verify` (or
++     `domain_connect`) completes to `ATTACHED` performing exactly one
++     add POST and one verify POST in total (no re-add on the second
++     call) — proves `domain_connect`'s "prepare + verify when DNS is
++     ready" compatibility framing in the module docstring.
++   - `domain_connect` alone (no separate prepare beforehand) remains a
